# Dependencies and build caches at the repo root.
#
# `app/` has had its own .gitignore since the beginning; the root had none, so
# a stray `npx --prefix app` run from here wrote a vitest results cache into a
# root node_modules and git tracked it. That one file then turned up as an
# uncommitted change after every test run, for the rest of time.
node_modules/
.vite/

# Python, for the pipeline.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Local secrets. .env.example is committed; nothing else is.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.DS_Store
*.log

# Scratch the Supabase CLI writes when it runs.
supabase/.temp/

# Rendered lesson video.
#
# The MP3s beside these are committed — they are the product, 46MB for four
# courses, and every student streams the same file. The MP4s are not: they are
# derived from those MP3s plus the cue list, re-rendered by
# `pipeline/lessons.py <course> --remotion` whenever they are wanted, and a
# single 1080p unit is larger than the entire audio library. See
# video/README.md.
app/public/audio/lessons/**/*.mp4

# And the shorts, for the same reason and more so: one per flashcard is 278
# files across the four courses.
app/public/audio/shorts/

# And the documentary cuts, which are 28 minutes each.
app/public/audio/documentary/

# And the character-sheet layouts. Both files here are derived from
# `pipeline/personas.mjs` — the spec by `persona-sheet.mjs`, the picture from
# the spec — and re-drawn by `node pipeline/persona-sheet.mjs --all --layout`
# in a few seconds. Committing them would be committing the preset twice, and
# the second copy is the one that goes stale.
app/public/video/personas/
